0	109	Marta Kos (Slovene pronunciation: [ˈmáːrta ˈkóːs]; born 28 June 1965) is a Slovenian diplomat and politician.
110	216	She served as ambassador to Germany from 2013 to 2017, and as ambassador to Switzerland from 2017 to 2020.
217	329	Since December 2024, she is the European Commissioner for Enlargement in the second von der Leyen's Commission.

329	418	From April to September 2022, she was one of the vice presidents of the Freedom Movement.
419	563	Ahead of the 2022 presidential election, she was the candidate of the Freedom Movement for president of Slovenia until her withdrawal in August.
564	637	Following the withdrawal she resigned as Freedom Movement vice president.
638	794	Following resignation of Tatjana Bobnar as Minister of the Interior she also resigned from the Freedom Movement stating that it is not her party anymore.



794	896	Early life and career
In her youth, Kos was a record-holding Yugoslav and Slovenian swimming champion.
897	1073	She studied journalism and joined the sports division of RTV, and later moved to Germany where she worked for Deutsche Welle and as Bonn correspondent for RTV starting in 1993.
1074	1201	From 1997 to 1999, she served as director of the Slovenian government information office and as spokesperson of the government.
1202	1285	In 2000, she was appointed vice president of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry.

1285	1425	In 2013, the government of Alenka Bratušek appointed her Ambassador to Berlin, Germany, as part of a political quota (non-career diplomats).
1426	1485	In 2017, she was appointed Ambassador to Bern, Switzerland.
1486	1679	In 2020, she resigned as ambassador due to disagreement with the government's foreign policy, as well as accusations of mobbing and consequential internal control over the work of the embassy.

1679	1746	In 2022, she announced her candidacy for President of the Republic.
1747	1864	In unexplained circumstances, she resigned from her candidacy and resigned as vice-president of the Freedom Movement.
